the FCC is cracking down on conspiracy  theorists alex jones and they're not the  only ones but is it a violation of free  speech chief congressional correspondent  Mike Emanuel has our report from Capitol  Hill right now infowars.com has been  taken down the FCC has shut down  controversial host Alex Jones's liberty  radio and slapped it with a fifteen  thousand dollar fine which it won't pay  but the Commission says it's been  operating without a license since at  least 2013 and Jones has a conspiracy  theory about what went down oh it's a  private company they can take you down  no this is just so they are  exponentially I believe beta testing  ahead of a big event civil unrest  fascination at trump who knows what the  false flag is a group of false flags  today the FCC Chairman appeared before  the Senate Commerce Committee Rajat  pices Jones's station was taken down  because he was violating the law not  because of the nature of his speech it  is important to make clear that our  pirate radio enforcement efforts  including this one have nothing to do  with the content that pirate radio  stations air the FCC Chairman says this  type of enforcement doesn't typically  get much attention normally our pirate  radio enforcement efforts don't make  national news but this one has because  the pirate radio station in question was  airing Alex Jones as his show Jones is  also getting squeezed by Apple removing  his podcasts facebook youtube linkedin  spotify even pinterest and there's also  an issue with twitter after he posted  this video calling for people to get  their battle rifles ready against the  media chief executive jack dorsey says  he's hoping to modify Jones's tone by  putting him in a Twitter timeout so  whether it works with in this case to  change some of those behaviors and  change some of those actions I don't  know but this is consistent with how we  enforce what President Trump has  complained about Twitter shadow banning  prominent Republicans in calling it a  discriminatory and illegal practice  while Jones with his conspiracy theories  is an easy target there are some who  worried this is a slippery slope where  people with different viewpoints could  be silenced  Brett McMahon  on the hill Mike thanks
 

